&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technology Finance partners across Infrastructure, Engineering, and Product teams to plan, forecast, and manage the cost of running Airbnb&#39;s cloud and AI platforms. The team sits at the intersection of finance and technical infrastructure, translating usage trends — cloud compute, storage, and AI spend — into forecasts and cost narratives that inform company-wide investment decisions. Key cross-functional partners include Engineering, Procurement, and FP&amp;amp;A, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns the understanding, forecasting, and influencing of Airbnb&#39;s total cloud and AI spend, spanning traditional AWS infrastructure and AI. Success looks like a cost narrative leadership can act on, and identified efficiency opportunities that measurably bend the cost curve without degrading product or employee experience. This includes leading planning cycles (FY26 close-out, FY27 guidance) and driving month-over-month rigor in cost variance analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the monthly/weekly cloud and AI cost forecast, reconciling actuals against plan and explaining variance drivers to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track AI spend by category and by model/provider mix, flagging shifts in usage or pricing that affect the forecast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Infrastructure and AI Platform engineering teams to size, validate, and prioritize efficiency initiatives (model routing, token optimization, provider migration).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own migration-tracking reporting (e.g., provider mix shifts, cost impact of model changes) and ensure the underlying data is traceable back to source systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and present cost updates to a broad, senior audience, translating technical usage data into clear financial narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and quantify new cost efficiency opportunities in partnership with technical stakeholders, and track them through to landed savings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run monthly and ad hoc reviews with Finance and Tech leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 years of finance, FP&amp;amp;A, or cost management experience, ideally including direct exposure to cloud infrastructure costs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with AI/ML infrastructure costs strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and maintain complex financial models and forecasts in ambiguous, fast-changing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record partnering with engineering/technical teams to translate usage data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
