&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Airbnb&#39;s Data Infrastructure organization builds the systems that store, move, and transform data across the company. Our Data Movement &amp;amp; Transformation (DMT) group is building a single, unified platform for moving data between Airbnb&#39;s storage systems, replacing dozens of one-off tools with one reliable, well-supported way to get data where it needs to go. This platform is the foundation for Data as a Service, a top-level infrastructure initiative at Airbnb.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ingestion team is the front door to DMT. We build and operate two managed, multi-tenant platforms that move data out of Airbnb&#39;s online databases for offline processing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SpinalTap:&lt;/strong&gt; near real-time change data capture (CDC) streaming to Kafka for every Aurora and UDS table at Airbnb.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DBExports:&lt;/strong&gt; periodic full-table snapshots and mutation exports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teams across Airbnb depend on these systems, including payments, fraud detection, financial reporting, search, messaging, notifications, and machine learning. Reliability, performance, and scale are the product. You&#39;ll work closely with DMT&#39;s other teams, which own real-time streaming infrastructure, pipeline orchestration, and schema management, and you&#39;ll have the chance to work across the broader platform&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be hands-on (code, design, test) and work with partner teams, internal customers, and leadership to deliver multi-month projects on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate large-scale CDC and batch export systems that run across every online database at Airbnb.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the architecture of DMT&#39;s unified data movement platform while it&#39;s being built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, performance, and efficiency of systems that critical business functions depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make it easier for engineers at Airbnb to get their data into offline systems without needing to be database or pipeline experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in on-call and raise the operational bar for a platform that other teams build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and operating large-scale backend distributed systems, such as data ingestion, streaming, CDC, storage, or data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with streaming systems like Kafka, and with how databases capture and publish changes (binlogs, Debezium, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own and go deep in a complex codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining, analyzing, and debugging production systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clean, readable, testable, and maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills in a remote-working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and a track record of delivering on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building managed or multi-tenant platforms used by other engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MySQL/Aurora, schema evolution, or large-scale batch data processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
